Phase 3 - Generate persistent volumetric density
  Depends on: Phase 2.
  Outcome: native weather produces stored 3D shape that all later ray consumers can share.
  [x] Capture certified native descriptors synchronously; retain no borrowed native texture across
      callbacks. Observe content changes without treating publication generation alone as a reset.
  [x] Implement generation-only native cuboid overlap/coverage, connected faces and perturbation.
      Store cell-average extinction; thin cell intersections contribute under the selected contract.
  [x] Implement bounded density jobs and content revisions; coalesce observations without resetting
      pending age. Update neighbor influence; pure wind translation retains unchanged material data.
  [x] Publish complete regions/boundaries after barriers, preserve unaffected data and expose spatial
      age differences. Handle out-of-band changes using the selected replacement policy.
  [x] Update conservative occupancy with each density publication, including the hardware-filtering
      footprint. Revoke unsafe old empty certificates before new occupied density becomes readable.
  [x] Verify declared coverage math, finite stored units, publication ordering and change retention
      with focused fixtures; no procedural approximation/image gate. Update density documentation.
  [x] Completion: density and safe occupancy are persistent and inspectable; no ray shader needs
      native geometry or procedural detail to determine visible/transport density.

Phase 3 verification
  Source mapping: generation/observation/work/occupancy tasks -> proposal / Selected representation
    (Native inputs, Generation/publication, Metadata/budgets, Acceleration); inherited native borrowing
    -> PBR.Clouds.md / Borrowed map and Ownership; source/enablement boundaries -> atmosphere publication
    and Rendering.Enablement.md. Current generation documented under Stored density-volume resources.
  Private typed density operations implement certified validation, one owned circular snapshot,
    overlap/detail generation, bounded fair/oldest jobs, indirect submission, filtered occupancy repair
    and successful-only completion. Native borrows are cleared after synchronous work; initial snapshots
    freeze until their full density publication. Unchanged content/wind retains density and ages.
  Second review and independent completion audit passed. Final cached Release build 11.03s, 0 errors
    (169 existing warnings), all 508 production/592 fixture binaries reused. Two density GPU facts passed,
    none skipped, 770ms. Three unchanged domain/storage facts passed in the prior focused run: five total.
  Receipts: artifacts/cloud-volume-density-final-build.log, artifacts/cloud-volume-density-final-tests.log,
    artifacts/test-results/cloud-volume-density-final.trx; retained prior tests in cloud-volume-density.trx.
  The analytic-overlap check permits only enclosing half-representation endpoints; no approximation,
    image or convergence threshold. No packaging/game run, GPU timing or appearance qualification.
  Tiny synchronous envelope/completion-summary reads and occupancy-repair costs remain to measure.
    Transport, final traversal and live selection/view rendering remain later work.

Phase 4 - Traverse stored density and schedule retained work
  Depends on: Phase 3.
  Outcome: bounded ray traversal and fair lighting jobs are ready for both transport solvers.
  [x] Implement the selected initial traversal (coarse DDA unless Phase 1 explicitly revised it),
      retaining state across block boundaries. Support zero direction components, anisotropic cells,
      negative rays, finite edges and circular addressing with forward progress.
  [x] Skip only certified empty support; preserve actual integration lengths and the selected occupied
      sampling rule. Avoid root restarts and silent work-limit truncation of admitted rays.
  [x] Implement separate bounded direct/diffuse queues after density publication. Prioritize new/
      changed content and active/visible stale work, with fair offscreen service and persistent ages.
  [x] Propagate nonlocal density demand conservatively, initially domain-wide if selected. Coalesce
      once per update; retain dirty state and actual completed revisions until successful work.
  [x] Handle light direction, intensity/environment, activation and refinement demand independently.
      Fog/exposure/camera motion must not clear compatible volume history.
  [x] Verify traversal coverage/progress, filter-support safety, fairness/work limits and failed-work
      stamps with focused contract checks. Document behavior; no full performance matrix here.
  [x] Completion: traversal is bounded and conservative, and queued work cannot become falsely fresh
      through selection alone or indefinitely starve due to repeated content changes.

