Phase 5 - Retain direct illumination through stored density
  Depends on: Phase 4.
  Outcome: published direct transmission is reused across views and frames.
  [x] Implement selected direct integrals using density textures and traversal exclusively. Store solar/
      lunar transmission; honor the finite domain and label any selected transport-distance truncation.
  [x] Dispatch only relevant-source work; prioritize activation, retain compatible direction-stale
      results and apply current source intensity later without recomputing unchanged transmission.
  [x] Publish successful region results/revisions after barriers; missing illumination uses the selected
      finite fallback without hiding occupied clouds. Failure cannot certify partial output as current.
  [x] Verify physical integration arithmetic, finite values, source activation/intensity behavior,
      disabled compiled paths and publication through focused existing abstractions. Update docs.
  [x] Completion: direct lighting consumes published density only and remains reusable under compatible
      source changes with honest age/dependency metadata. Incremental validation receipts are recorded.

