      and empty batches. Do not reuse timings from the undersampling traversal as a matched baseline.
  [x] Audit CloudVolumeUpdates, CloudVolumeDensity, CloudVolumeWork and CloudVolumeDiffuse dependencies.
      Separate CPU-required admission/domain decisions from GPU producer-consumer ordering. Identify
      each fence/readback and why it is needed; retain asynchronous admission where CPU results are
      necessary without turning every downstream stage into a separate rendered-frame step.
  [x] Chain work selection, direct tracing/completion and diffuse copy/gather/completion through the
      existing command stream with explicit storage/image/texture/indirect-command barriers. Include
      density generation/occupancy in that chain wherever its validated admission permits. Remove
      intermediate fences used only to sequence GPU consumers; do not imply backend async-compute
      overlap or move graphics commands to an unsupported CPU thread/context.
  [x] Remove the intermediate CPU diffuse-job-count decision. Use GPU-produced counts/conditional
      work to suppress empty tracing and unnecessary whole-field copying, while preserving coherent
      old-field reads, untouched texels, encoding/scale compatibility and correct swap/publication
      semantics. Do not swap in an uninitialized destination when GPU-selected work is empty.
  [x] Accumulate arithmetic/completion status on the GPU and inspect it after the final completion
