    Gaussian, with reassociated float32 rounding; no approximation tolerance was introduced.
    It trades one near-depth exponential for division/multiplication and saves nothing beyond
    the third-bucket saturation distance. A fixed across-interval recurrence does not apply:
    bin=log(1+adjustedDepth/30) is nonlinear, while clipped DDA intervals have variable lengths.
    A varying recurrence still needs changing log/exp terms and adds retained state. Vectorizing
